Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: watchdog: retain the tethered warm boot state

A tethered kernel inherits initialized hardware rather than power-on
state. Retain the board-selected warm handoff state so probe and
shutdown do not discard resources needed by the incoming kernel.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/apple,wdt.yaml | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/apple,wdt.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/apple,wdt.yaml
index ca4cf01db..a8179c208 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/apple,wdt.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/apple,wdt.yaml
@@ -13,6 +13,12 @@ allOf:
   - $ref: watchdog.yaml#
 
 properties:
+  apple,tethered-boot:
+    type: boolean
+    description: |
+      A SoC reset leaves the tethered OS. The restart handler refuses warm
+      and soft reboot modes; cold reboot retains the normal SoC reset.
+
   compatible:
     oneOf:
       - items:
